{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>If a thread.</b> A head ornament, as our rabbis taught: ״חוטין שבראשי הבנות״ in tractate Shabbat (65a) — they are silk threads with which they tie their hair." "<b>A shoelace.</b> A leg ornament. Another interpretation: <b>if a thread</b> — from which all garments are made, meaning whether a large thing or a small one." "<b>And if I take from all that is yours.</b> When I left my father's house, HaShem promised to enrich me; it is better that I not <b>take from all that is yours</b>, and when I become wealthy I will attribute the wealth to the one to whom wealth and honor belong."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:14.294087102Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}